  "hypotheses": {
    "H1_shortcut": "In main_r3, a model shows the shortcut if block_first latest accuracy is at least 20 points below general_nonblock. Confirmed if a majority of evaluated models show it (10 of 18 with joint models).",
    "H2_error_identity": "Pooled over models and main_r2..r4, at least 80% of block_first errors return the first replacement.",
    "H3_trained_layout_sanity": "In main_r1 (training distribution), block_first latest accuracy is at least 95% in all but at most one evaluated model.",
    "H4_rule_specificity": "Among models showing the shortcut in main_r3, block_after_one_unrelated, run_broken_before_latest and initial_then_run are each within 10 points of general_nonblock in a majority of those models (the failure needs the unbroken run from slot 0).",
    "H5_gap_control": "Open question, either result is reported: among models showing the shortcut, does the block_first deficit (>=20 points) persist at query distance 12 and 16, where filler separates memory from query? Persisting implicates the write run; vanishing implicates memory-query adjacency or absolute position."
